MetaMask eth-phishing-detect (DBAD v1.2)
-----------------------------------------
https://github.com/MetaMask/eth-phishing-detect

Parry's engine/brand_match.js reimplements, from that project's publicly
described algorithm, an allowlist-first reversed-label suffix match and a
graded fuzzy brand-domain matcher (bounded edit distance, homoglyph
normalisation, subdomain/hyphen brand-token injection, and TLD-swap
detection). Only the algorithm shape was consulted — brand lists, weights,
and thresholds are Parry's own.

jsQR (Apache License 2.0)
--------------------------
https://github.com/cozmo/jsQR

engine/qr.js vendors jsQR v1.4.0 verbatim (unmodified, pure JavaScript, no
WASM, no network access) as the on-device QR-code decoder behind
ScamShield's quishing (QR-phishing) detection — decoded http(s) payloads are
scored through ScamShield's own existing verdict engine; jsQR itself
contributes no detection logic of its own.

